e","H1961":"to be","H5850":"crown","H8597":"beauty","H3027":"hand","H6797":"turban","H4410":"kingship","H3709":"palm","H430":"God","H559":"to say","H5750":"still","H5800":"forsake","H776":"country/planet","H8077":"devastation","H3588":"for","H2657":"Hephzibah","H1166":"Married","H2654":"to delight in","H970":"youth","H1330":"virgin","H1121":"child","H4885":"rejoicing","H2860":"son-in-law","H5921":"upon","H3618":"bride","H7797":"to rejoice","H2346":"wall","H6485":"list","H8104":"obey","H3117":"day","H3915":"night","H8548":"continually","H2142":"to remember","H853":"[Obj.]","H408":"not","H1824":"quiet","H5414":"give","H3559":"prepare","H7760":"make","H8416":"praise","H7650":"to swear","H3225":"right","H2220":"arm","H5797":"strength","H518":"if","H1715":"grain","H3978":"food","H341":"enemy","H8354":"to drink","H5236":"foreign","H8492":"new wine","H3021":"be weary/toil","H622":"to gather","H398":"to eat","H1984":"to shine","H6908":"to gather","H2691":"court","H6944":"holiness","H5674":"to pass","H8179":"gate","H6437":"to turn","H1870":"conduct","H5971":"people","H5549":"to build","H4546":"highway","H5619":"to stone","H68":"stone","H7311":"to exalt","H5251":"Banner","H2009":"behold","H8085":"hear","H413":"to(wards)","H7097":"end","H1323":"daughter","H3468":"salvation","H935":"come","H7939":"wages","H854":"with","H6468":"wages","H6440":"before","H1350":"redeem","H1875":"to seek","H5892":"excitement"},"ccc":{"0":[1611],"4":[219]},"cccp":{"219":"__P16#","1611":"__P51#"},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Rest, as long as God grants me life, or till I behold the Saviour; or Cyrus, the figure of Christ. (Calmet) — True preachers will not be silent on account of any threats, but will labour for the Church, 2 Timothy ii. (Worthington)"],["haydock",2,null,"jerome","One. No profane historian mentions what Cyrus did for the Jews; but all the world knows how much Christ has favoured his Church. (Calmet) — Name. Thou shalt be no longer the rebellious Jerusalem, but the spouse and chosen people, the Church of Christ. (St. Ignatius of Antioch, ad Magnesians) (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Hand. Chaldean, “before.” Hebrew, “by the protection.”"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Forsaken. Yet the synagogue was again rejected, at the death of Christ. The promises naturally relate to his Church. (Calmet) — Inhabited. Protestants retain the Hebrew words Chephtsi-bah, “my delight in her,” and Beulah, (marginal note) “married.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Dwell. Hebrew, “marry.” They shall be attached to their country. — Thee. He shall love thee as a bridegroom does one whom he has lately married. Christ never abandons his virgin spouse. (Calmet) — Isaias speaks of some state of the Jews which has not yet taken place. (Houbigant)"],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Watchmen; priests and prophets, (Matthew ii. 1., and Psalm cxxxiii. 2.; Calmet) or angels. (St. Jerome; St. Bernard) — The synagogue has been long destitute of guides, but the Catholic Church has an uninterrupted succession of watchful pastors. — Mindful whose duty it is to remind him of his promises, and to recite the Church office. (Calmet) — Hebrew mazcirim, monitors, 2 Kings viii. 16. (Haydock) — In these faithful watchman the Church is always visible. (Worthington)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Hand; inviolably, Deuteronomy xxxii. 40. The Persians deemed this oath most sacred. (Calmet) — Darius, just expiring, said to Polycrates, “By thee I give this right hand to Alexander,” (Plut.[Plutarch?]) that he may revenge my death. — Wine. The Church cannot be deprived of her faith or of her God."],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","People, that they may return to Judea, and be converted to Christ. (Calmet)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Work the redemption of mankind. (Haydock) — Though Cyrus was a figure of Christ, he was as much beneath him as earth is below heaven, Zacharias ix. 9. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"jerome":["Jerome",1,1,420,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#jerome"]}}